{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## NOTE: the three preceding entries are IDENTICAL DUPLICATES of one session log — read any one\n\nAuthor error, recorded rather than hidden. I wrapped `session-log append` in a retry loop guarded by\na verification predicate that searched `rebar list` for the log's title. **`rebar list` excludes\n`session_log` tickets by design** (its output contains only story/bug/task/epic), so the predicate\ncould never match, every attempt read as a failure, and the same 10151-byte entry was appended three\ntimes. The store is append-only and there is no comment-delete, so the duplicates stand.\n\nTwo lessons, both instances of the same root error I logged four times inside the entry itself:\na verification that CANNOT succeed is indistinguishable from a failure, and I did not check the\npredicate against a case known to exist before trusting it to drive a retry loop. `session-log append`\nhad in fact reported `created: false` each time — i.e. it appended to the existing log successfully.\n**I retried against my own broken check instead of reading the command's output**, which is precisely\nthe failure mode the entry above warns about."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785900707026581001,"uuid":"9944c613-ac34-43fe-b1e2-b2d363d2fbd5"}